ef 17592186473962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d883981-f066-5218-a1bf-dd76574de46e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42469" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has proportional columns\n- **II.** $A$ has identical rows\n- **III.** $A$ has a zero row\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134407 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133912 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba7d7bc9-77ef-583c-8caa-22315aad7aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$, $|B|$, and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392523} {:answer/id #uuid "23f02ed7-eb83-5988-a1ca-ee80eac659ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392524} {:answer/id #uuid "d767aec8-a44c-5175-bbcd-b71f577015fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392525} {:answer/id #uuid "ee7ae539-44fc-5d03-b8b9-5a5b498db62e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392526} {:answer/id #uuid "3737a2a5-a57d-571a-a651-f2cad4ee3049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d767aec8-a44c-5175-bbcd-b71f577015fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392525} :answer-field/id #uuid "00ef10bc-f305-5726-8271-949923025e38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cee2c526-7176-535a-81f7-173bfaefecec" :question/math-academy-id "q-42882" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|B|=1\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=12\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-poin